            "description": "An appropriation of money with its own authorization ceiling, the portion of it placed under obligation, and the portion actually expended. Questions about how much money is left to obligate, whether authorization covers what has been committed, or where the effort will run out of money before it runs out of work target this class. Its three quantities are a LADDER - each is a subset of the one above it - which is what distinguishes it from a requirement compared against a supply.",
